From f857ce0c275975d30613b898a0e931d20f10c6b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:07:46 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/24] kcm_componentchooser: page first, application lists
 filled afterwards

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). mimeapps.list writes, terminal kcfg keys, KLauncher call and behaviour
are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- Kirigami.Form/FormGroup -> Kirigami.FormLayout. First section (Web browser, Email client, Calendar, Phone
  Numbers) has no title; sections Multimedia, Documents, Utilities keep their names and order.
- New link at the end, section "Other file types": "Configure File Associations..." opens kcm_filetypes
  (ia/duplicates.md "Default Applications & File Associations": this page owns the common defaults, File
  Associations stays the per-type editor). The existing "Configure Manually..." in Details stays.
- Combo boxes are disabled and show "Loading..." until their list is filled; a busy indicator appears after
  150 ms. Combos get accessible names and buddies.
- The ChooserFormEntry component is now ChooserRow (ColumnLayout for FormLayout); unused unsupportedMimeText() removed.
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_componentchooser.tsv (outer repo). 19 inventory rows kept, 0 lost (--strict).

Speed cause: KcmComponentChooser::load() called ComponentChooser::load() 13 times synchronously
(kcm_componentchooser.cpp), each running KApplicationTrader::query over every installed service and
serviceSupportsMimeType() with a QMimeDatabase lookup per advertised mime type of every service
(applicationmodel.cpp:46, componentchooser.cpp). On top, the page's warning bindings called
unsupportedMimeTypes / mimeTypesNotAssociated (KApplicationTrader::preferredService per mime type) for all 13
choosers as soon as each model was reset. Fix:
- load() now queues the 13 choosers in page order and fills one per event-loop turn (QTimer::singleShot(0)),
  so the first frame no longer waits; new properties ComponentChooser::loaded and KcmComponentChooser::loading.
- The file type warnings return empty until the chooser is loaded.
- serviceSupportsMimeType() looks the target mime type up once per call instead of once per advertised type.
Numbers: before 0.5 CPU ~2.2 s to first frame (build/bench/clean/before-slow.tsv); after: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-013, HIG-017, HIG-019, HIG-020, HIG-023, HIG-047, HIG-058, HIG-062.

Not built yet (freeze).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
